      "writtenOn": "2026-10-09T19:43:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Changing from .resolve() to .absolute() here is risky. If the path provided is a symlink to a directory in a git repository, absolute().parents will follow the lexical path of the symlink rather than the actual directory structure. This will fail to find the git repository if it resides in a parent of the target directory but not in a lexical parent of the symlink.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 70,
