      "writtenOn": "2026-10-09T19:43:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "git apply --numstat output for renames uses the format `added\\tdeleted\\tpath/to/{old \u003d\u003e new}.c`. Simply calling Path() on the third column will result in an invalid path like `{old \u003d\u003e new}.c`. You need to parse the `\u003d\u003e` syntax or use git apply --summary to get renames in a more parsable way.",
